{
  "note": "How HPCivil3d/ mirrors HPAutoCad/ (ADR-01 option A). MirrorTests read this file. Rules: (1) `tokens` are applied to the AutoCAD text IN ORDER (exact strings — identifiers, constants and the few one-line differences); (2) lines between `// civil-only: begin` and `// civil-only: end` (C#) or `<!-- civil-only: begin -->` … `<!-- civil-only: end -->` (XAML/XML) exist only in the Civil file and are stripped before comparing — a block may only ADD lines, never replace one; (3) `versionPatterns` are replaced by a placeholder on both sides so a version bump on either product is not drift; (4) `civilOwnedFiles` are Civil-specific and not compared line by line; those hand-ported from an AutoCAD file are listed in `ownedCounterparts` with the sha256 of the AutoCAD text (CRLF folded, BOM dropped) they were ported from — when AutoCAD changes that file the pin fails until the change is ported (or declined) and the hash re-pinned; (5) every source file of both bridge trees must appear in `mirroredFiles`, `civilOwnedFiles` or `ownedCounterparts`. Blank lines, trailing whitespace, CRLF and the BOM are ignored.",
